1
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:03,640
Nan'an 1-Day Tour (Old Street & Ancient House Food, for tourists with tight schedules)

2
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:06,840
Nan'an 1-Day Tour (Old Street & Ancient House Food, for tourists with tight schedules)

3
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:09,320
Why is it so noisy downstairs?

4
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:11,640
We've gone viral!

5
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,760
It's not us.

6
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:14,650
It's Tang Yi.

7
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,480
Today at the shop,

8
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:19,740
several customers came asking him for makeup and styling.

9
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:22,960
It's the video we went out to shoot the other day.

10
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:23,920
After you fell asleep,

11
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:26,520
I edited it and posted it online for promotion.

12
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:29,080
So did we go viral or did Mr. Tang?

13
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,560
Hurry up, wash up and let's go.

14
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,680
Stop talking about Mr. Tang all day.

15
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:35,479
What about Mr. Tang?

16
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:36,640
It's you.

17
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:39,520
Always talking about Mr. Tang.

18
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,440
Where are we going?

19
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:46,880
Did you just hear this part,

20
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:47,680
sister?

21
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,800
Although we didn't go viral,

22
00:01:51,039 --> 00:01:52,880
at least we gained something.

23
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,600
Three orders.

24
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:55,880
Today,

25
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,660
we've already received deposits for three orders.

26
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,120
Thank you, Mr. Zhang.

27
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,520
Hurry up, pack up and let's go.

28
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,380
Stop dawdling.

29
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:14,840
What did you just call me?

30
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:21,620
Profiteer.

31
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:40,560
What do you mean?

32
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,240
Why is the first client so difficult?

33
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,040
Wait a minute.

34
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:46,680
No, aren't these just mochi?

35
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,800
The sizes are different,

36
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,040
and they are more expensive than downstairs.

37
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:50,640
It's like this,

38
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,440
Mr. Zhao.

39
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,880
These Yingdu mochi

40
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,480
use the best ingredients.

41
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:54,920
Yes.

42
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,800
And it's completely handmade.

43
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,680
Yes, that's right.

44
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:00,480
It's also a local intangible cultural heritage snack here.

45
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,320
So this...

46
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:03,320
You don't need to tell me all this useless stuff.

47
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:04,400
I don't buy it.

48
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:10,520
What's wrong? Do you think I'm too demanding?

49
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,160
No, Mr. Zhao.

50
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,440
Our company's lifelong goal

51
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,680
is that the customer is god.

52
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:18,520
Learn from this little brother.

53
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,130
Go ahead with your work.

54
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:31,880
Starting work

55
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,520
next Monday is fine.

56
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,640
But I have a quick question.

57
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,960
Is it possible

58
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,680
to increase

59
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,010
the housing allowance?

60
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,480
No problem at all.

61
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,079
What do you mean?

62
00:03:45,079 --> 00:03:46,680
They are not the same thing.

63
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:47,440
What does he want?

64
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,920
Might as well press it out with a machine.

65
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,000
He's nitpicking.

66
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,240
No,

67
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,400
I'm not

68
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:53,320
complaining.

69
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:54,720
I...

70
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:57,880
No,

71
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,210
why are you telling me not to go?

72
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,400
Did you say it was handmade? Hands?

73
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,320
Who cares.

74
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:06,570
They are guests.

75
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:13,720
Can you tell?

76
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,320
They are of different sizes.

77
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,320
Look at the flour.

78
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,980
It's unevenly coated.

79
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:18,839
Full of flaws.

80
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,680
Sir, we just said it was handmade.

81
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:24,280
By hands.

82
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:24,920
How could I not know?

83
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,080
What she means is,

84
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:27,480
this mochi,

85
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,400
because it's handmade,

86
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,600
the sizes will vary.

87
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,120
But it tastes the same.

88
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,250
Please try it first.

89
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:51,720
No.

90
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,900
The soybean powder

91
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,930
isn't evenly coated on both sides.

92
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,500
And look at this shape.

93
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:02,760
It should be oval.

94
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:11,200
It tastes better this way.

95
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,240
Yes, Mr. Zhao.

96
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:19,280
If you really don't like it, just eat less.

97
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,680
Let's go to the next stop.

98
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,280
Watch your attitude.

99
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,810
Mr. Zhao, we're leaving first.

100
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:27,920
Let's go.

101
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,800
Why the long face?

102
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,890
Weren't you happy to pick up the client this morning?

103
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:44,000
It's not strange to see this expression on my sister's face.

104
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,280
If Zhang Yang did it,

105
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,000
it wouldn't be easy.

106
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,120
Have a pear.

107
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,420
My sister doesn't like pears.

108
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,880
Then what do you like to eat?

109
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:55,800
She likes to eat

110
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,560
oranges without pith.

111
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:58,800
Xinyue,

112
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:01,140
you guys really had a rough day today.

113
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:03,000
I took a client to eat braised noodles,

114
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,480
added some red mushrooms,

115
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,680
which turned the soup pink.

116
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:08,440
He insisted I brought him noodles with food coloring

117
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:09,640
and wanted to complain.

118
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,400
I said oyster omelets taste better with crispy edges.

119
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,560
He insisted I ruined it and was just making excuses,

120
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,080
and wanted to complain about me.

121
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,560
I took him to eat Popiah.

122
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:18,680
There were some chives inside.

123
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,320
He didn't say he doesn't eat them!

124
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,920
He insisted on blaming me,

125
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,720
and wanted to complain about me.

126
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,280
He said the name 'Pigu Noodles' isn't elegant,

127
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,480
and wanted to file a complaint about it.

128
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,360
He is not here for a tour at all.

129
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,820
He is just here to nitpick.

130
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,680
You saw it yourself today.

131
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:42,480
Along the way,

132
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,159
he made 8 or 9 phone calls.

133
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,720
He has a PhD.

134
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:46,880
He still hasn't found a job,

135
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:48,800
so it's understandable that he is anxious.

136
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,680
That's because he's so picky,

137
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,320
that he lost all opportunities.

138
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:52,960
I'm a tour guide.

139
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,360
I'm not his punching bag.

140
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,240
Look on the bright side.

141
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,720
It's only for three days.

142
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,520
Three days will pass quickly.

143
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:00,960
Just bear with it.

144
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:03,340
It's bad for your health to hold it in.

145
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,480
How about taking the client to

146
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,080
the Zheng Chenggong Memorial Hall?

147
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:10,960
It has a good meaning,

148
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:13,090
and we can encourage him along the way.

149
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,720
Not bad. You can only win if you fight for it.

150
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:30,360
Bad-tempered sister.

151
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,080
Cool down.

152
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,520
Idiot.

153
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,480
I'm so angry.

154
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,320
It's so sour.

155
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,920
Zheng Chenggong Memorial Hall.

156
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:03,880
Yes, sir.

157
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:07,220
Zheng Chenggong, a native of Nan'an,

158
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,760
is a national hero who expelled the Dutch colonists

159
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,760
and recovered Taiwan.

160
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:13,920
He is also an important part of Nan'an's history.

161
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,580
Are you reading from a script?

162
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,130
With your professional skills...

163
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,440
Be a bit more expressive.

164
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:22,960
You are absolutely right, sir. I'm sorry.

165
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,400
I will definitely give you an expressive explanation later.

166
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,000
All right. Let's go.

167
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:27,600
Okay.

168
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:28,650
Let's go.

169
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,600
Come, follow this way.

170
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,880
Hurry up and hold the flag up.

171
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,340
Mind the steps.

172
00:08:36,159 --> 00:08:39,620
Everyone knows Zheng Chenggong's feat of recovering Taiwan.

173
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:42,080
But few people know

174
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,400
that before that,

175
00:08:43,559 --> 00:08:45,420
he also suffered a tragic defeat.

176
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:48,920
Then tell me,

177
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:50,520
how did this hero fail?

178
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,120
Heroes are human too.

179
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:54,080
Life has its peaks,

180
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:55,720
and it has its valleys, right?

181
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,320
After that defeat,

182
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,680
his trusted aides advised him to retreat overseas temporarily

183
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:00,940
to plan for the future.

184
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,480
The tables will turn.

185
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,160
Don't bully the young and poor.

186
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,760
But he didn't agree.

187
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,920
He chose to return to his hometown immediately

188
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,200
to regroup.

189
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:11,800
He was 35 that year.

190
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,080
He was no longer a youth.

191
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:15,760
Men remain boys until death.

192
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,360
So, that led to his later heroic act

193
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:22,280
from 1661 to 1662,

194
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,840
where he spent ten months

195
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:25,120
expelling the Dutch colonizers

196
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:27,720
and recovering Taiwan.

197
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:28,760
Great.

198
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,260
Come to Nan'an, and you will succeed.

199
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,920
You only win if you fight.

200
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,760
You only win if you fight.

201
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,320
You always say you only win if you fight hard.

202
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:45,120
So only those who win are heroes?

203
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,600
What about those who don't?

204
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,440
What are they?

205
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:50,840
What am I then?

206
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,200
A client.

207
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,650
Is this the time to be smart?

208
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,040
Let me tell you.

209
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,840
If it weren't for the free spot you gave me,

210
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,160
I wouldn't even have come.

211
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,690
Do you know why I'm unhappy?

212
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,960
Too utilitarian.

213
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,320
There are so many hurdles in life.

214
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,960
You're only successful if you overcome them.

215
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:09,520
If you can't, it means you didn't work hard enough.

216
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,760
So one fall ruins your whole life, right?

217
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:12,600
I really don't know

218
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,360
what you two are lecturing me about.

219
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,200
From yesterday till now,

220
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:18,200
everything you two

221
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,760
arranged for me

222
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,240
has failed to satisfy your client.

223
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:23,890
You've already fallen.

224
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:27,160
If one fall in life is the end,

225
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,090
Then life would be ruined long ago.

226
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:34,960
Is that how you talk to a client?

227
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,120
I didn't mean to insult him.

228
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,640
I was just stating a fact.

229
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:42,640
Look, everyone has to learn to walk when they are young.

230
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,400
And you're bound to fall when learning.

231
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,160
He said,

232
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,960
life is ruined once you stumble.

233
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:50,720
Then there are few whose lives wouldn't be ruined.

234
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,520
He's so picky about everything.

235
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,720
It's really annoying.

236
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,720
Okay, you're always right.

237
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,200
But he's the client.

238
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,920
He has the right to be picky.

239
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:01,920
Look, once the tour ends tomorrow afternoon,

240
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:03,960
if he files a complaint and reports you,

241
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:04,890
what will you do?

242
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:05,930
What will you do?

243
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:08,000
Why don't you apologize first?

244
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,860
Is there any other way besides apologizing?

245
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:12,880
I did.

246
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,920
Ask him. I apologized three times,

247
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,250
but he didn't accept it.

248
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,720
If my sister were here,

249
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,200
she would definitely scold him worse than I did.

250
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:20,840
Why are you bringing up your sister all of a sudden?

251
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,170
What's wrong with that?

252
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,600
She's my sister.

253
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,040
Okay.

254
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:26,900
You are all my sisters, all right?

255
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,040
Since when do you have so many sisters?

256
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,840
She's my sister.

257
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,400
You're baffling.
